          "Write the escalation log authority in plain words: what may change, by whom, after what evidence, with what confirmation. A delegated change without a scope can outlive the project that justified it. Keep emergency authority narrow, time-bound, and followed by a review note in the same case. Formatting and labels may be corrected without approval; the underlying escalation log value may not. The November 2 escalation log recovery test should record the restore point and the renewal risk lead time result.",
          "Customer success manager may prepare, compare, label, and route escalation log; support lead keeps the decision that changes the onboarding tracker. A delegated change without a scope can outlive the project that justified it. Separate the right to request, prepare, and publish; merging them causes most confusion. A role change should trigger a review of the onboarding tracker permissions and queue routing. For the November 2 review at Customer Success Managers, record the escalation log check with the onboarding plan and the QBR completion result."
