          "The source is recorded before the action, because order is what makes the escalation log trail believable. A request that arrives through a side channel is copied into the queue before work begins. Keep queue columns stable: request, evidence state, owner, next action, due time, destination check. The handoff note should be readable by someone who has not seen the case. At Customer Success Managers, keep the onboarding plan attached to the escalation log case and record the reopen rate observation date.",
          "Work is sorted by evidence state rather than arrival time, so complete requests move and incomplete ones return with a precise question. If the same escalation log request appears twice, link the duplicate to the surviving case. The daily routine should make the next action obvious without a meeting. Use the same status words in the queue and the daily note. The November 2 evidence trail for escalation log should show the source version and the customer sponsor decision."
